  "title": "Partial List Coloring",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture Let $G$ be a simple graph with $n$ vertices and list chromatic number $\\chi_\\ell(G)$. Suppose that $0\\leq t\\leq \\chi_\\ell$ and each vertex of $G$ is assigned a list of $t$ colors. Then at least $\\frac{tn}{\\chi_\\ell(G)}$ vertices of $G$ can be colored from these lists.",
